  "result": "Type-checks cleanly and the full test suite passes. Three fixes made:\n\n1. **`src/server/repositories/organization-repository.ts`** — `updateOrg` was unioning the incoming `enabledFlagOverrides` with the currently-stored set, so a removal (patch with a smaller set) was always merged back to the superset. Now it replaces with the patch's set when provided.\n2. **`src/server/services/feature-flag-service.ts`** — `toggleFlag`'s guard exempted any `strategy.kind === \"plan\"` flag from the overridability check, letting plan-only, non-overridable flags (e.g. `webhooks`) be turned on. Now it simply rejects when `!definition.overridable`.\n3. **`src/lib/feature-flags.ts`** — `isEnabled` honored a stored override even when the flag definition isn't overridable. Now the override branch only applies when `definition.overridable` is true, so a stale/invalid stored override has no effect and the flag falls through to its own strategy rule.",
